## Recommended backend fixes

These are not required for the Angular UI, but I recommend applying them manually.

### Protect the score endpoint

The current score route accepts any authenticated `gameId`. In [gameRouter.js](./routers/gameRouter.js), add ownership filtering to the `Rounds.findAll()` query:

```js
const rounds = await Rounds.findAll({
  where: { gameId },
  attributes: ["distance"],
  include: [
    {
      model: Games,
      as: "game",
      attributes: [],
      where: {
        gameId,
        userId: req.user.userId,
        status: "completed",
      },
    },
  ],
});
```

Also reject incomplete scores:

```js
if (
  rounds.length !== 3 ||
  rounds.some((round) => !Number.isFinite(Number(round.distance)))
) {
  return res.status(404).json({
    error: `Did not find a completed three-round game for gameId: ${gameId}`,
  });
}
```

### Fix duplicate-guess responses

The current duplicate-guess branch sends a response from inside the Sequelize transaction and then the outer handler tries to send another response. That can produce `ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT`.

Replace:

```js
return res
  .status(409)
  .json({ error: "That round has already been guessed" });
```

with:

```js
const duplicateGuessError = new Error(
  "That round has already been guessed",
);

duplicateGuessError.status = 409;
throw duplicateGuessError;
```

Then update the catch block:

```js
} catch (error) {
  console.log(error);

  const status = error.status === 409 ? 409 : 500;
  const message =
    status === 409
      ? error.message
      : "Failed to log guess";

  return res.status(status).json({ error: message });
}
```

