</details>

The cause is the flex layout: `.guess-panel` has a fixed height, so when the hint card appears, the flexible `<app-guess-map>` shrinks to make room.

Reserve a fixed hint area so the map keeps the same height before and after clicking Hint.

In [game-board.html](./frontend/src/app/components/game-board/game-board.html), replace the current hint block:

```html
@if (hintText(); as hint) {
  <aside class="ai-card" role="status" aria-live="polite">
    <h3>Location hint</h3>
    <p>{{ hint }}</p>
  </aside>
}
```

with:

```html
<div class="hint-slot">
  @if (hintText(); as hint) {
    <aside class="ai-card" role="status" aria-live="polite">
      <h3>Location hint</h3>
      <p>{{ hint }}</p>
    </aside>
  }
</div>
```

Then append this to [game-board.css](./frontend/src/app/components/game-board/game-board.css):

```css
.guess-panel {
  overflow: hidden;
}

.hint-slot {
  flex: 0 0 7.5rem;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.hint-slot .ai-card {
  margin-top: 0;
}
```

This reserves approximately 120px for the hint even before it is displayed. The map will remain the same size after the hint loads, and unusually long hints will scroll inside the reserved area.

The existing `.guess-map { overflow: hidden; }` is fine; that rule only clips the map’s own contents and is not causing this issue.

